@*
 * FILE ROLE: Injects shared directives (namespaces, tag helpers) into every
 *            view in the Views/ folder tree — no per-view repetition needed.
 * SECTIONS IN THIS FILE:
 *   1. @using — namespace imports for all views
 *   2. @addTagHelper — tag-helper registration
 *@

@*
 * SECTION 1: @using — NAMESPACE IMPORTS
 *
 * @using directives in _ViewImports.cshtml apply to every .cshtml file in
 * the same folder and all sub-folders.
 *
 * With <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings> in the .csproj, ALL
 * namespaces must be explicit — even in Razor views.  _ViewImports.cshtml
 * is the right place to centralise view-layer imports.
 *@
@using LayoutsSectionsPartials.Models
@using LayoutsSectionsPartials.ViewComponents

@*
 * SECTION 2: @addTagHelper — TAG-HELPER REGISTRATION
 *
 * @addTagHelper <namespace-or-wildcard>, <assembly>
 *
 * This line makes all ASP.NET Core built-in tag helpers available in every
 * view:
 *   <a asp-action="Index" asp-controller="Page">Home</a>
 *   <form asp-action="Create" method="post">…</form>
 *   <input asp-for="Title" />
 *   <label asp-for="Title" />
 *   <span asp-validation-for="Title" />
 *
 * The wildcard * means "all tag helpers found in that assembly".
 *
 * To also enable the ViewComponent tag-helper syntax (<vc:navigation />),
 * the same @addTagHelper *, <YourAssembly> is required — the Razor compiler
 * scans for ViewComponent classes and generates the tag helper descriptor.
 * That syntax is covered in → 08. Tag Helpers.
 *@
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
